[
  {
    "comment": "The beehive kiln is the vitrification rung: whatever comes out of it is stoneware. Each beehivekiln entry is a JsonItemStack, and JsonItemStack.Resolve applies an embedded `attributes` object onto the resolved stack's NBT, so stamping the tier is pure JSON \u2014 no code touches the beehive at all. Every existing entry is left exactly as it is: this is addmerge onto the entry, never a replace, so all four vanilla colours at all four door counts survive unchanged. That regression is verification step 10. Porcelain is absent from this file by design \u2014 it is a real variant, not an attribute, and its own beehivekiln map belongs to porcelain-ware-raw.json.",
    "file": "game:blocktypes/clay/raw/bowl",
